# GitHub and git — no Cursor branding

When committing, pushing, or opening pull requests for this project:

## Never include

- Any `Co-authored-by:` trailer naming Cursor or an IDE agent — **never**, even if commit integration adds it automatically
- `Made-with: Cursor`, `Made with Cursor`, or any Cursor/IDE/agent attribution
- Commit trailers, footers, or tags that mention Cursor, Copilot, or the agent
- Casual or promotional tone in commit/PR text

## Commits (agent workflow)

1. Write a professional message only (conventional commits or user-requested text).
2. Commit with plain `-m` flags — do **not** append co-author, made-with, or sign-off lines.
3. After `git commit`, run `git log -1 --format=full` and confirm **no** `Co-authored-by:` line exists.
4. If Cursor injected a trailer:
   - **Not pushed yet:** `git commit --amend` and remove the trailer, then verify again.
   - **Already pushed:** tell the user and offer `git commit --amend` + `git push --force-with-lease` only if they approve.

```text
# ❌ BAD (reject / amend before push)
Add pit boss CCTV.

Co-authored-by: <IDE agent>

# ✅ GOOD
Add pit boss CCTV wall and self-service camera registration.
```

## Pull requests

- Title and body: professional summary + test plan only
- No IDE branding, co-author lines, or "generated by" disclaimers

## Pushes

- Do not push a commit that still contains Cursor branding
- If a hook or IDE integration re-adds trailers on amend, strip them again before push
